# 2026-11-20: the Galaxy S26 (SM-S942Q) LiteRT-LM GPU rows of LFM2.5-350M, LFM2-700M, LFM2-2.6B,
# LFM2-2.6B-Exp and Qwen3.5 0.8B for the dashboard page, in one set of runs, every file on LiteRT-LM's public prebuilt
# Android binaries: the side build public-0.19.0-20261029 (gs://litert/binaries/latest/android_arm64/litert_lm/,
# objects 2026-10-29, the binary's version string 0.19.0, the GPU accelerator compiled in, not built here;
# android/engine-pins.json litert-lm.public-0.19.0-20261029).
# Task: native-benchmark-1024x256 = litert_lm_advanced_main --benchmark, prefill forced to exactly 1024 tokens,
# decode 256, context 2048 (methodology/protocol-gemma4.md "The spec").
# Files: the Hub files of 2026-11-20, each read at the repo revision on its comment line and checked against the Hub
# API's LFS sha256 (size and sha256 below). Model id = <Hub repo>/<variant>, variant = the file name after
# "<model>_" up to ".litertlm". file= is the checked copy's path from the repo root (the job runs the runner there;
# .dashboard/ is not in git): run_cell.ensure_model hands the model id to hf_hub_download, which takes no three-part
# id (the form of the earlier <repo>/<variant> rows, e.g. matrices/ctx-ladder-q06-e2-ynnpack-a-android.cells).
# First row = the Android llama.cpp session anchor row of matrices/anchors.cells byte for byte
# (the job's anchor phase runs both Android rows of anchors.cells first).
# Cooldowns as in docs/dashboard-cells-v1.md and matrices/dashboard-protocol1024-v1-android.cells:
# the runner's 120 s up to Qwen3.5 0.8B (no cooldown=), cooldown=300 on the six rows of the two 2.6B models (the
# weekly rows of the 2B-and-up models carry 300; the page's rows of these two models today are card figures of
# 2026-10-13, one process of three iterations each, which name no rest between launches). No runs= (3 runs per row,
# round by round).
# Run from the repo root with the phone reserved for the whole run (the job does not reserve or free it):
#   BENCH_SITTING=1 python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py s26 --cells matrices/lfm2-qwen35-s26-public-android.cells --suffix lfm2-qwen35-public --once --hold-held-by <pid that reserved the phone> --no-post
# The campaign name holds `dashboard`, and its LiteRT-LM rows have the model ids, task and context of the page's rows from
# matrices/lfm2-qwen35-s26-pregpu-*.cells, so the page reads their records there once results/summary has them.
android llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF short-chat anchor=1 runs=3 file=Qwen3-0.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf
